</div></div><a href="#" class="closebtn">×</a></div></div></nav><div class="site-inner"><div class="content-sidebar-wrap"><main class="content" id="genesis-content"><nav id="breadcrumbs" aria-label="breadcrumbs"><span><span><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/">Home</a></span> &gt; <span><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/category/coffee-drinks/">Coffee Drinks</a></span></span></nav><article class="post-11395 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail category-coffee-drinks category-recipe mv-content-wrapper entry" aria-label="Pumpkin Cream Cold Foam"><header class="entry-header"><h1 class="entry-title">Pumpkin Cream Cold Foam</h1>
<p class="entry-meta">Published: <time class="entry-time">Jul 27, 2024</time> by <span class="entry-author"><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/" class="entry-author-link" rel="author"><span class="entry-author-name">Ana</span></a></span> · This post may contain affiliate links · <span class="entry-comments-link"><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/pumpkin-cream-cold-foam/#comments">2 Comments</a></span></p></header><div class="entry-content"><div class="wprm-recipe wprm-recipe-snippet wprm-recipe-template-emk-snippet-buttons"><a href="#recipe" data-recipe="11396" style="color: #ffffff;background-color: #000000;border-color: #ffffff;border-radius: 3px;padding: 3px 8px;" class="wprm-recipe-jump wprm-recipe-link wprm-jump-to-recipe-shortcode wprm-block-text-normal wprm-recipe-jump-inline-button wprm-recipe-link-inline-button wprm-color-accent">Jump to Recipe</a>
<a href="https://www.pinterest.com/pin/create/bookmarklet/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.espressomykitchen.com%2Fpumpkin-cream-cold-foam%2F&amp;media=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.espressomykitchen.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F07%2FEspresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-steps-3.jpg&amp;description=Pumpkin+Cream+Cold+Foam&amp;is_video=false" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" data-recipe="11396" data-url="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/pumpkin-cream-cold-foam/" data-media="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-steps-3.jpg" data-description="Pumpkin Cream Cold Foam" data-repin="" role="button" style="color: #ffffff;background-color: #000000;border-color: #ffffff;border-radius: 3px;padding: 3px 8px;" class="wprm-recipe-pin wprm-recipe-link wprm-block-text-normal wprm-recipe-pin-inline-button wprm-recipe-link-inline-button wprm-color-accent">Pin Recipe</a></div>
<p>This pumpkin cream cold foam recipe has the perfect amount of pumpkin and sweetness. It's so easy to make at home and it's the perfect dupe to the Starbucks Pumpkin cold foam for half the price.  This recipe is one of my favorites as soon as we enter pumpkin season. If you love this homemade pumpkin cold foam then you will also love this <a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/chocolate-cream-cold-brew/">easy chocolate cold foam </a>and this <a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/matcha-strawberry-latte/">strawberry cold foam</a>. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" fetchpriority="high" src="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-4.jpg" alt="Pumpkin cream cold foam over an Iced coffee topped with cinnamon" data-skip-lazy class="wp-image-11419" srcset="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-4.jpg 1200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-4-200x300.jpg 200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-4-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-4-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-4-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-4-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Why you will love this recipe! </h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Not overly sweet</li>



<li>Makes the perfect fall weather cold foam for your iced coffee</li>



<li>This cold foam recipe is half the cost than buying it at your favorite coffee shop </li>
</ul>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What is cold foam?</h2>



<p>Cold foam is a milk base frothy topping that is similar to whipped cream, but not as stiff as whipped cream. Cold foam is more creamier and lightweight. It's commonly poured over iced coffees, cold brews and iced lattes. Cold foam can be easily made with a hand frother, hand mixer, blender or shaking a mason jar vigorously.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Ingredients you'll need </h2>



<div class="wp-block-group"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p><strong>Pumpkin puree  </strong>- The main ingredient for this cold foam. Make sure it's the 100% pumpkin and not the pumpkin pie mix<br><strong>Brown sugar</strong> - to add some sweetness<br><strong>Heavy cream </strong>- for that creaminess <br><strong>Milk -</strong> extra creamy oat milk or any milk of choice that froths really well <br><strong>Pumpkin Pie Spice </strong>- for that extra pumpkin flavor<br><strong>Ground Cinnamon </strong>- 1 shake is all you need for topping<br><strong>Coffee</strong> - cold brew, latte, or coffee of choice<br><strong>Vanilla syrup</strong> - (optional) 2 pumps of store bought vanilla syrup to stir into  the cold brew to make it a copycat Starbucks Pumpkin cream cold foam brew<br><strong>Tools -</strong><a href="https://amzn.to/49OMrva" rel="nofollow"> hand frother,</a> (my personal favorite) blender, mason jar with a lid or electric hand mixer works too</p>
</div></div>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1800" height="1200" src="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-ingredients-1.jpg" alt="Pumpkin cream cold foam ingredients" class="wp-image-11408" srcset="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-ingredients-1.jpg 1800w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-ingredients-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-ingredients-1-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-ingredients-1-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-ingredients-1-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-ingredients-1-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1800px) 100vw, 1800px" /></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How to make Pumpkin Cold Foam</h2>



<div class="wp-block-group"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p><strong>Step one</strong> - Start by adding the heavy cream, milk, pumpkin puree, brown sugar, and ground pumpkin pie spice in a small cup. Using a <a href="https://amzn.to/49OMrva" rel="nofollow">hand frother </a>froth for about 30 seconds or until you have reached a thick frothy consistency and set aside</p>



<p><strong>Step 2</strong> In a tall glass add iced cubes and pour in cold brew or your favorite iced latte. </p>
</div></div>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-3 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="683" height="1024" data-id="11413" src="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-1-683x1024.jpg" alt="Pumpkin cold foam being frothed with hand frother" class="wp-image-11413" srcset="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-1-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-1-200x300.jpg 200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-1-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-1-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-1-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-1.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 683px) 100vw, 683px" /></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="683" height="1024" data-id="11414" src="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-2-683x1024.jpg" alt="Iced cold brew being poured in a glass" class="wp-image-11414" srcset="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-2-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-2-200x300.jpg 200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-2-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-2-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-2-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cream-cold-foam-steps-2.jpg 1200w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 683px) 100vw, 683px" /></figure>
</figure>



<p><strong>Step 3</strong> Pour the pumpkin cold foam over your favorite iced coffee and sprinkle some ground cinnamon on top and enjoy!</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" src="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-steps-3.jpg" alt="Pumpkin cream cold foam being poured over an iced cold brew" class="wp-image-11409" srcset="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-steps-3.jpg 1200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-steps-3-200x300.jpg 200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-steps-3-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-steps-3-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-steps-3-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Espresso-My-Kitchen-pumpkin-cold-foam-steps-3-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Substitutions</h2>



<div class="wp-block-group"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p><strong>Brown sugar </strong>- You can substitute with cane sugar, maple syrup or agave nectar. <br><strong>Milk</strong> - I like using extra creamy oat milk, but you can use any milk of choice. You can skip the heavy cream, but the consistency won't be the same. Using both heavy cream and milk gives it that delicious frothy texture without being overly stiff like whipped cream. If you go the <strong>non-heavy cream route</strong> I suggest you use extra creamy nut milks and barista style milks as from my experience those milks tend to froth really well. <br><strong>Pumpkin Pie Spice </strong>- You can use ground cinnamon instead or make your own pumpkin pie spice at home. <br><strong>Coffee  - </strong> not feeling like drinking cold brew with your cold foam? I like pouring this easy pumpkin cream foam over my favorite <a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/brown-sugar-shaken-espresso/">brown sugar shaken expresso</a>, or iced lattes and iced americanos too! Any iced coffee of choice will really work perfectly.</p>
</div></div>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Storing</h2>



<p>For any cold foam leftovers you can store in the refrigerator in an airtight container for up to 3 days and froth again using a hand frother before serving.</p>


<div id="recipe"></div><div id="wprm-recipe-container-11396" class="wprm-recipe-container" data-recipe-id="11396" data-servings="1"><div class="wprm-recipe wprm-recipe-template-emk-chic-template"><div class="wprm-container-float-right">
